Q1. What is a Procedure in PL/SQL?

Interview Ready Answer

A Procedure is a named PL/SQL block that performs a specific task.

It is stored in the Oracle database and can be executed multiple
times whenever required.

Purpose

• Reuse business logic.
• Reduce code duplication.
• Improve maintainability.
• Perform database operations.

Examples

• Insert employee record.
• Update salary.
• Delete records.
• Generate reports.

======================================================================

Q2. Why do we need Procedures?

Interview Ready Answer

Procedures are used to store reusable business logic inside the
database.

Advantages

• Code reusability.
• Better maintainability.
• Reduced network traffic.
• Improved security.
• Easier application development.

======================================================================

Q3. What is a Function in PL/SQL?

Interview Ready Answer

A Function is a named PL/SQL block that performs a specific task
and must return exactly one value using the RETURN statement.

Functions are mainly used for calculations, validations and
returning computed results.

Purpose

• Perform calculations.
• Return computed values.
• Reuse business logic.
• Improve maintainability.

======================================================================

Q4. Why do we need Functions?

Interview Ready Answer

Functions are used whenever a program needs to perform a calculation
or business logic and return a value to the caller.

Examples

• Calculate employee bonus.
• Calculate total salary.
• Validate user input.
• Find tax amount.

======================================================================

Q5. Difference between Procedure and Function.

Interview Ready Answer

Procedure

• Performs a specific task.
• Return value is optional.
• Can return values using OUT parameters.
• Mainly used for INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE operations.

------------------------------------------------------------

Function

• Performs a specific task and returns a value.
• RETURN statement is mandatory.
• Returns exactly one value.
• Mainly used for calculations and validations.

